{"description":"Write an HTML surface's body. Pass any of `html` / `css` / `js`; omitted fields stay unchanged. Pass empty string to clear. The surface renders in a sandboxed iframe with no access to Dock cookies, storage, or parent DOM, and scripts do not run there today: inline `<script>` and the `js` field are stored but never execute. Build pages that work without JavaScript; for interaction use CSS (`:hover`, `:focus`, transitions), `title=` attributes for tooltips, and `<details>`/`<summary>` for expanders. External CDN fonts and CSS (Google Fonts, Tailwind CDN, Fontsource), video, audio and CSS animations are fine. Text, numbers and charts go in the `html` itself. Per-field caps: html 256 KB, css 200 KB, js 200 KB, total 600 KB. The sanitizer is allowlist-based: standard HTML/SVG elements (including `<canvas>`, forms, `<style>`, `<script>`, `<link>`) and `id`/`class`/`style`/`aria-*`/`data-*` attributes are kept; anything off the allowlist is removed \u2014 e.g. `<iframe>`, `<object>`, `<embed>`, `<meta>`, `<base>`, custom elements, inline `on*=` event-handler attributes, `javascript:` and `data:text/html` URIs. Inline `on*=` handlers are removed and `<script>` does not run, so nothing script-driven will work. Call `validate_html` first: `parsed.htmlRemoved` lists exactly which tags / `tag[attr]` would be removed. Layout: Dock renders the surface EDGE-TO-EDGE (full-bleed) inside the workspace \u2014 the surface itself is the frame. Do NOT put `border-radius`, an outer border, or a drop-shadow on the root/outermost element unless the owner explicitly asked for that framing, or the specific design genuinely needs it; keep the page root flush and apply rounding to inner cards only. DESIGN LANGUAGE: Dock injects a base stylesheet into every surface \u2014 semantic tokens + a small component kit \u2014 that automatically follows each VIEWER's light/dark theme. USE these by default and never hardcode a color, including inside SVG: color SVG with classes or var(--dock-*) in CSS, not hex in fill=/stroke=. A hardcoded color looks broken for a viewer on the other theme (a dark surface for a light-mode viewer, and vice-versa). Tokens: var(--dock-canvas|surface|surface-muted|border|border-strong|text|text-2|text-muted|accent|accent-ink|data|data-strong|good|warn|crit), var(--dock-radius|shadow|gap); font is Inter via var(--dock-font). Component classes: .dock-card, .dock-stat/.dock-stat-value/.dock-stat-label, .dock-delta.up|.down, .dock-badge.good|warn|crit|neutral|accent (add a <span class=\"dot\"></span>), .dock-btn(.primary), .dock-table (use td.name for the primary cell, .dock-num for tabular figures), .dock-grid, .dock-eyebrow, .dock-row, .dock-avatar, .dock-field + .dock-input, .dock-bars/.dock-bar(.hot). Put .dock-num on any number so it aligns. This is a DEFAULT floor: override layout and type freely with your own CSS (nothing in the baseline is !important); colors stay on the tokens. CHARTS: draw them as static inline SVG in `html` (bars, lines, axes, labels and the numbers in the markup). Never rely on a script to render content: the page must read the same with scripts off, and to `get_html`. Requires editor role. Returns a short receipt, not the page: { surface_slug, url, updatedAt, bytes: { html, css, js }, sanitized } \u2014 `sanitized` lists any field you sent that the sanitizer changed on write. Before you share the surface's link, read it back with `get_html` and confirm the content and numbers you meant are there.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"css":{"description":"CSS source. Applied inside the sandbox iframe. You can also `<link rel=\"stylesheet\">` external stylesheets from any HTTPS CDN (Tailwind CDN, Google Fonts, icon kits); CSS works, scripts do not.","type":"string"},"html":{"description":"HTML body. Sanitized server-side (smells stripped; `<script>` and `<link>` are kept, but scripts do not run in the surface today, so use `<link>` for CDN stylesheets and fonts only). Use `validate_html` first for a pre-flight check.","type":"string"},"js":{"description":"JS source. Stored alongside html/css but not executed: html surfaces render with scripts off today. 200 KB cap (matches the top-level `update_html` description; the server enforces `HTML_SURFACE_LIMITS.jsBytes` = 200_000).","type":"string"},"slug":{"description":"The workspace slug.","type":"string"},"surface_slug":{"description":"Optional html surface slug. Omit to write the primary html surface.","type":"string"}},"required":["slug"],"type":"object"},"name":"update_html"}
